oir 2 own
// expect OIR2-B9.1 terminator:8:8
// §6.3c (Fable, tightening of KEEPER, #862): the shape of B9-cold-shared-cache, with the Future first passed through
// `Passer.pass`, which takes it and returns it. Its duty comes back to main in the call's result packet as a
// returned entry (own's output of `let g = Passer().pass(Maker().make("x"))`). A plain split then names a view of
// the Future's outcome (`@view`, cache-owned) and would extract the duty: refused, as for a cache-owned duty. Only
// an admissible selection leaves a returned entry silently.
